==English==

===Etymology===
Related to earlier {{m|en|hand over hand}}, this phrase originally referred to a speedy method of climbing up or hauling on a rope.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-hand over fist.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Quickly or in great [[quantity]], especially in reference to earning [[money]].
#: {{syn|en|hand over hand}}
#: {{coi|en|to make money '''hand over fist'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1880|author=Robert Louis Stevenson|title=The Letters of Robert Louis Stevenson|volume=I|chapter=[[s:The Letters of Robert Louis Stevenson Volume 1/Chapter IV|chapter 4]]|passage=Are you coming over again to see me some day soon? I keep returning, and now '''hand over fist''', from the realms of Hades: I saw that gentleman between the eyes, and fear him less after each visit.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888|author=Rolf Boldrewood|title=s:Robbery Under Arms|chapter=[[s:Robbery Under Arms/Chapter 39|chapter 39]]|passage=Now, since cattle had risen and meat and all to such a price, he was making money '''hand over fist'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Connecticut Yankee|passage=He was a live man and a brisk talker, and had two journeymen and three apprentices, and was doing a raging business. In fact, he was getting rich, '''hand over fist''', and was vastly respected.}}
#* {{RQ:London Valley of the Moon|passage=Why, those Dalmatians are showing Pajaro apples on the South African market right now, and coining money out of it '''hand over fist'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Sinclair Profits|passage=Now we are in the War and our business is booming, we are making money '''hand over fist'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=8|passage=Still it’s the same fish perhaps old Micky Hanlon of Moore street ripped the guts out of making money '''hand over fist''' finger in fishes’ gills can’t write his name on a cheque think he was painting the landscape with his mouth twisted.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2009/06/its-time-to-tax-college-sports/18699/|title=It's Time to Tax College Sports|work=The Atlantic|date=2009-06-03|author=Conor Clarke|passage=And while pulling in dollars '''hand over fist''' might have some educational value, I doubt it's what Congress had in mind.}}

